{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794790000000-engineer-d1-r14-companion-subset-retention.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md collab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md collab/yang-clojure/1794810000000-engineer-d1-r17-reconstruction-package.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md collab/yang-clojure/1794820000000-engineer-d1-r19-symlink-fix.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-17 09:39:07 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-17 04:39:07 EST\n\nThe requested publication is **incomplete**. I recorded the worktree findings in [the r14 findings file](/home/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1794790000000-engineer-d1-r14-companion-subset-retention.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md).\n\nThe subset extraction was interrupted after producing a partial store; I removed that incomplete artifact. The companion and verification result remain blocked by missing recipe, provenance, image-verification, and complete two-lane trace evidence. The full-store retention owner remains pending designation.\n\nThe standing battery passed **58 tests and 708 assertions**. Kondo reported **0 errors and 1 warning** across the inherited battery. The frozen v1 file’s SHA-256 remains unchanged. No commit was made.Completed-GMT: 2026-11-17 09:45:07 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-17 16:45:07 +07\n\nDelivered a partial prerequisite for the executable recipe: [correspondence_dependency.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/src/cljc/yang/correspondence_dependency.clj) stores and retrieves byte-preserving, content-addressed dependency bundles. It does **not** establish or execute the compiler dependency closure.\n\nThe requested items 1–2 checkpoint remains incomplete. The named r14 findings and architect rulings, along with the Jupiter retained store described in the handoff, are absent from this checkout. The separate laptop store was not substituted for them.\n\nFocused tests passed: 9 tests, 76 assertions. Kondo reported zero errors and warnings, and the frozen v1 table hash remains unchanged. No full oracle suite ran and nothing was committed.\n\nThe worktree findings and exact remaining work are recorded in [r15 findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md).# D1 r17 — assembly linkage pilot, reconstruction package incomplete\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. This is a **partial continuation below the requested steps 1–3 checkpoint**. No execution manifest, retained runtime/package, standalone reconstruction entrypoint, later corpus reconstruction, companion publication, or verification result was produced. Nothing here establishes D1 reliance. The existing stores and outcomes remain unchanged; the row-lane-only and bounds/execution restrictions remain in force.\n\nThe executable-closure adjudication `1794805000000-architect-d1-executable-closure-adjudication.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` is now present and was read. It explicitly permits a later reconstruction package while distinguishing reproducibility from historical runtime attestation; successful replay cannot invent missing admissions or expansion events. The earlier r17 note saying that adjudication and r14 were absent is superseded: both are now present. The two earlier architect ruling files and continuation-4 named in the handoff were not found under their supplied names here; the recorded r5 numeric-fidelity implementation is not a substitute for those original texts. The Jupiter r9b store is not present on this laptop.\n\n## Completed partial work\n\nThe inherited `yang.correspondence-text` docstring correctly labels its profile as **serialization metadata**, not an executable reconstruction profile. Its stored value is unchanged. The earlier r16 inventory's inference that original runtime capture must precede *any* later reconstruction is corrected by the new ruling; original-process provenance remains a separate, unresolved claim.\n\nIn `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, `d1-assemble` now names the existing direct assembly of instrumented forms and call, library inclusion, and compiler options. `kernel-compile` uses that same composition. The producer-side `d1-check-reconstruction!` now rebuilds that program and options from the retained forms and call and compares them with the retained program/options using the existing order-, metadata- and numeric-fidelity relation before replay. A small test checks refusal of a changed call and changed options. This narrows the compilation/hash split in **that producer-side pilot only**. It shares the assembler and compiler loaded by the invoking checkout; it does not reconstruct fixture adaptation from verified context sources and does not establish independent verification or an executable closure. The separate `verify-retained-fixture!` remains unchanged and still compiles the retained program without this assembly check.\n\nThe prior local observation `target/d1-r17-classpath-inventory.json` describes the current `clojure -Spath -M:test` invocation: 154 ordered entries (144 files, 10 directories), with sizes and SHA-256 for regular files, and Java 21.0.2 on macOS aarch64. Its SHA-256 is `a6b29f8306f845829c409705a5e97e03541e05824d2b0882302eb2b8ba87ecb0`. It is a scratch observation, not retained dependency bytes or a manifest. It does not inventory directory contents or retain the runtime, identify all source/resource/native dependencies, or prove isolation. It is not evidence of the historical process.\n\n## Unresolved acceptance blockers\n\n1. The current text-profile equality check in `test/yang/correspondence_verification.clj` still selects the invoking checkout's compiler, not a verified manifest-driven fresh process. No manifest or executable reconstruction profile exists.\n2. The producer-side assembly check above is not the required independently reconstructed fixture/source/adaptation-to-root chain. The existing retained-fixture gate still has the original split; no corpus was evaluated under the new check.\n3. Constructor names in the existing independent gate still come from the producer snapshot; verified context-source inputs must instead derive them and be compared with the snapshot.\n4. The six retained roles do not publish an execution manifest or an expansion-applicability/context record. The observed direct composition merits investigation but absence of events alone is not a bypass proof; historical expansion remains uncertain.\n5. `yang.correspondence-dependency` remains a byte-bundle primitive and makes no completeness claim. The new manifest, classpath ordering, runtime layout/modes/links, load/launch plan, transitive availability, supported-host refusal and isolated entrypoint still need implementation and validation.\n\nThe later reconstruction must fetch addressed source/resource and binary bytes and an addressed runtime, verify them after process exit, run without the producer checkout or ambient dependency caches, and compare every claimed chain output. It must reuse only retained admission coordinates supported by the facts and preserve missing history as incomplete. Derive classification inputs, publish the side artifacts, verify image derivations and complete lane evidence under a finalized adequate declaration, and publish a separate verification result. No existing roots or events should be adjusted to make replay pass.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe new focused assembly test was run red first (missing `d1-assemble`), then passed: 1 test, 3 assertions. The existing producer-side close/reopen replay test passed: 1 test, 6 assertions. The single live compilation against frozen site evidence passed: 1 test, 12 assertions. Kondo on the changed oracle test reported 0 errors and 0 warnings; `git diff --check` passed. The frozen v1 `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite, tagged lanes, or corpus run was executed.\n# D1 r19 — portable runtime link, observational content index\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. This is a partial continuation, below the requested items 1–3 checkpoint. The runtime archive's observed absolute link has been corrected and its restored JDK starts on this host. The dependency closure and launch configuration are not established. This is not a reconstruction package, D1 verification, or historical runtime attestation. No fixture, admission coordinate, event, root or outcome was changed. Existing bounds and row-lane restrictions remain.\n\n## Runtime\n\n`src/cljc/yang/correspondence_inventory.py` now normalizes absolute runtime symlinks that resolve within the captured distribution to relative links and refuses runtime links that resolve outside it; relative links with a lexical escape are also refused. It records the normalization policy in the runtime entry. Classpath capture is unchanged. This is an inventory helper, not a general safe archive extractor or a validator of executable closure.\n\nThe retained scratch observation `target/d1-r19-inventory.json` has SHA-256 `e9f1ccce6ed4c582d580285f46c1005cc9c9dbf91ff276095a2648e67ee71daf`. It references the original r18 ordered classpath archives and a new runtime object in `target/d1-r18-inventory-store/objects/3b625c942e1363e888139071ef608e0dc49e83694eaa85ff683b732077363673` (343,838,720 bytes). Comparison of the old and new runtime tar members found 519 entries with identical names, types, modes, sizes and regular-file bytes; the only link-text difference is `content/Contents/Home`, from `/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/java/21.0.2` to `..`. The runtime is therefore a normalized layout, not byte-identical to the original layout. A fresh process verified the r19 manifest's referenced object sizes and hashes.\n\nA red-first synthetic test captured a runtime whose Home link pointed to its original absolute root, deleted that root, extracted the archive elsewhere, and checked the link, bytes and executable mode. The initial implementation failed; the corrected implementation passes. A second red-first test checks refusal of an outside runtime link. For the actual JDK, after extraction to a temporary path, all 206 symlinks were relative and resolved inside the restored tree, and `Contents/Home/bin/java -version` succeeded as OpenJDK 21.0.2 on this Darwin arm64 host with a minimal environment. The original JDK remained installed during that actual-runtime execution, so this is not an OS-enforced no-access test; the separately checked link targets and synthetic deletion test are the evidence for this particular path independence. The temp extraction was removed. No cross-platform execution is claimed.\n\n## Classpath observation and limits\n\n`target/d1-r19-classpath-content-index.json` (SHA-256 `5938678ce98ecb2aa1fbbe4f515dd0d74aba76a2025c1f48c39f7d6275718ede`) lists, in classpath order, the referenced archive identity and the SHA-256, size and mode of each regular file, or link text and mode for links: 154 entries and 1,703 files/links. The index was computed from the captured tar contents, not coordinates or a fresh checkout. It is an observational scratch index, not a declared execution manifest; it does not identify indispensable members, establish source/resource/native completeness, constrain class/resource resolution or rule out ambient reads. Its bytes and the archives in `target/` have no durable retention owner or availability guarantee. The r18 classpath archives capture the earlier snapshot, not subsequent edits to the helper.\n\nThe absolute link fix and content index do not complete item 2. Still needed: determine the actual transitive source/resource, binary and native closure for the intended pipeline, retain and identify its exact bytes, and test that undeclared inputs are rejected. Item 3 still needs a versioned launch and build/load plan with entrypoint, ordered classpath/module path, JVM options, working-directory mapping, properties, environment, locale/encoding, initialization, stages and contracts. The existing inventory is not that plan. Durable retention/discovery with scratch-copy-before-open, substantiated expansion applicability, and a fresh isolated replay resolving compiler code from the verified package remain open. A later replay cannot establish historical runtime provenance or invent missing admission/expansion facts. The unavailable earlier architect ruling filenames and continuation-4 remain absent under the supplied names, as recorded in r17/r18; the present third ruling and available findings/declarations were consulted.\n\n## Validation\n\n`python3 test/yang/correspondence_inventory_test.py`: 4 tests passed, including the red-first cases above, ordered capture, corruption and nested-store refusal. Fresh-process archive verification and the runtime checks above passed. clj-kondo on the correspondence machinery/tests and `latte_oracle_test.clj` reported 0 errors, 0 warnings. `git diff --check` passed. Frozen `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite, tagged lane, corpus reconstruction, publication, or commit was run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
