{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794880000000-engineer-d1-r25-launch-closure-retention-replay.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r25 — explicit snapshot-probe launch and class-load observation\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. **Partial, below the requested items 1–3 checkpoint.** A versioned, fail-closed candidate launch plan now drives the r19 snapshot probe and was exercised successfully. It is a plan for that narrow experiment, not the reconstruction entrypoint or a complete launch configuration. Dependency closure, durable package retention, package-pinned expansion determination, and isolated retained-input replay remain unfinished. No D1 verification or historical runtime attestation is claimed. HEAD is detached at \"'`e4ac21142397d27bf6627121c29ddfb57a602970`, rather than on the branch name in the handoff. The retained stores and admission coordinates were not changed.\n\n## Candidate launch and validation\n\n`test/yang/correspondence_r25_launch_plan.json` (SHA-256 `591ac75bb9d12333a098b17500fcbab0f21646ea818447c1ee49bcd403065c04`) declares this experiment'\"'s target, r19 inventory digest, runtime-relative Java executable, all 151 retained ordered classpath indices (omitting 5–7), empty module path, JVM options, scratch working directory, environment and path-derived properties, locale, encoding, timezone, initialization order, entrypoint and expression hash. \"'`test/yang/correspondence_launch_plan.py` accepts precisely the supported version and 154-entry inventory, refusing alterations, extras and a relative scratch root. It builds a subprocess environment without inherited Java option variables; `HOME`, `TMPDIR`, `user.home` and `java.io.tmpdir` are mapped to new scratch directories. The executable, classpath and work directory point into the extracted snapshot. `test/yang/correspondence_r25_snapshot_launch.py` checks the r19 receipt digest and each selected archive'\"'s size and hash before extraction and invokes the plan in a fresh process.\n\nThese files explicitly scope themselves to the probe. The expression still arms two expander Vars after loading the macro namespace, then loads the oracle and invokes its existing fresh-admission static test; expected outputs are created by the same process. Platform facilities, JVM defaults and filesystem/network access are not fully declared or controlled, the Python bootstrap and plan remain worktree files rather than an addressed package, and the later r18/r19 snapshot is not historical process evidence. This is therefore not the ruling's complete launch configuration, closure proof, expansion determination or retained-input replay.\n\nBoth the initial candidate launch and an instrumented repeat passed **1 test / 6 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors**. The repeat added JVM class-load logging. \"'`1794880000000-engineer-d1-r25-class-load-summary.json` records 13,639 observed class-load events: 2,591 with six restored classpath locations as sources, 9,473 `__JVM_DefineClass__`, and other JVM/generated/platform source categories. The raw log is scratch at `target/d1-r25-class-load.log`, SHA-256 `13beb0d9c508b735aaccb06523048ce125bb1f1456e09e1ddef104d74b2a128f`. Its temporary directory was represented by both `/var` and `/private/var` on this host, so a few normalized summary strings begin `file:/private$SCRATCH/`; they refer to that scratch tree, not a declared external classpath. The six observed classpath locations do not prove the other entries unnecessary: Clojure source and resources, native loads, arbitrary file accesses and other stages are not covered by this class-load log. The r22 parser-directory and Netty-native exclusion experiment remains evidence only for its tested local path, not the complete reconstruction closure.\n\nA separate attempt to run `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` with a network-denying profile failed with `sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted` under the existing host sandbox. No escalation or alternative isolation was attempted. Consequently neither snapshot launch demonstrates refusal of checkout, caches or other ambient filesystem reads, and network isolation is not claimed.\n\n## Remaining work\n\nDefine the actual standalone reconstruction entrypoint, complete its manifest and pipeline contracts, enumerate and retain its transitive source/resource, binary and native needs, and enforce or audit the declared platform boundary against unavailable checkout and caches. Select an owner and durable discovery location for the addressed package, then demonstrate transitive retrieval after process exit using scratch-copy-before-open; the r19 snapshot and current logs remain scratch. For the pinned composition, substantiate the expansion bypass across its checked execution path, or retain the applicable context and events; neither local throw-arm probe proves historical behavior. Finally fetch and verify the retained package, launch the isolated entrypoint using package compiler code, reconstruct the retained input/adaptation through assembly and compilation/stamping, and compare all claimed outputs. Never manufacture admission coordinates, expected roots or historical events. Independent correspondence, image/trace evidence and bounded publication remain separate obligations.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe launch-plan tests passed 2 tests, including a red-first missing implementation and a red-first missing class-load-log option, with refusal of altered environment, path, classpath, expression and module-path fields. Snapshot archive safety tests passed 2 tests. clj-kondo on the manifest/dependency code and manifest/oracle tests reported 0 errors and 0 warnings. `git diff --check` passed. Frozen `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite, tagged lane, corpus replay, publication or commit was run. The earlier two ruling filenames and continuation-4 remain unavailable under the supplied names, as documented in r17–r24; the third ruling and available findings were consulted.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
